1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:10,068
WaterWatch is an offline field notebook that screens drinking water samples against federal reference levels, now with an SDG 6 clean-water equity lab built in.

2
00:00:10,238 --> 00:00:17,574
Everything runs in this one page, and its security policy forbids network connections, so nothing ever leaves the device.

3
00:00:18,194 --> 00:00:22,818
The School tap preset is a synthetic first draw at an older elementary school.

4
00:00:22,988 --> 00:00:31,075
Lead reads 24.6 parts per billion against the 10 part action level, while the same fountain after a flush reads 3.1.

5
00:00:31,245 --> 00:00:37,239
The report keeps both lead action levels on screen as context and never calls either one a safety verdict.

6
00:00:37,858 --> 00:00:43,571
The Industrial corridor preset, a synthetic private well, shows why the mixture matters.

7
00:00:43,741 --> 00:00:56,321
No single PFAS reading tops its own benchmark, yet four contributions sum to a Hazard Index of exactly 1.27, flagged above the limit of 1 beside the rule's one significant figure display.

8
00:00:56,942 --> 00:01:04,325
After the storm, a boil advisory pairs with a microbial detection and nitrate at 13.6 milligrams per liter.

9
00:01:04,495 --> 00:01:12,845
The guidance is bottled water first and the boil notice exactly as issued; the filter table warns a household filter is not an advisory fix.

10
00:01:13,015 --> 00:01:21,600
Sliding evaporation to 20 percent turns 13.6 into 17, because boiling off water only concentrates what stays behind.

11
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:27,563
The mixture and sensitivity lab compares all four presets against every benchmark at once.

12
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:34,408
It draws the Hazard Index breakdown and the per-contaminant ratio chart, then runs its deterministic checks in the page.

13
00:01:34,578 --> 00:01:37,195
All 32 in-page self-tests pass.

14
00:01:37,365 --> 00:01:43,519
The audited brief stamps one SHA-256 digest across the on-page line and every export.

15
00:01:44,139 --> 00:01:52,034
The SDG 6 lab grades the service ladder, the exceedance profile, and an illustrative water stress index for that same sample.

16
00:01:52,205 --> 00:01:58,478
Five low-cost interventions are priced against the grant budget, and the planner recommends the best modeled reach.

17
00:01:58,648 --> 00:02:06,066
A fit badge says plainly when an option covers the reported gaps, and an active advisory withholds every contaminant-fit claim.

18
00:02:06,236 --> 00:02:12,050
On the impact chart every marker is focusable, and every label declutters itself instead of colliding.

19
00:02:12,669 --> 00:02:17,851
One tap renders the whole lab in Spanish, indicators, planner and chart included.

20
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:28,970
The same recording run verified 695 of 695 Node tests, 56 of 56 headless audit checks, and zero honesty findings.

21
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:34,445
Everything shown was computed in the page during this drive, with zero network requests.

22
00:02:34,614 --> 00:02:37,138
WaterWatch. Know what is in your tap.
